{
 "design": "L233 does the destination geometry explain the asymptote? L217 refuted the SOURCE-population account BY HOMOGENEITY, so the leftward drift is a property of the pools' OWN in-wiring. A_inf = asym(per-cell means of v1) over a joint's pool cells, so this card asks what distinguishes the LEFT pool cells from their RIGHT homologs in v1: (a) raw in-degree, (b) in-MASS, (c) position in the Perron mode independent of both (the residual after regressing log v1 on log in-mass within pool), or (d) a small number of high-leverage cells. The card's own escape is registered: if (a)/(b) explain it, the whole A_inf family demotes to a description of the pools' in-mass asymmetry, which L205 already measured.",
 "prereg": "l233/PREREG.md",
